{{Politics of Okaiken}}

The {{Nihongo|'''Cabinet of Okaiken'''|内閣|Naikaku}} is the chief [[w:Executive (government)|executive]] body of the [[Government of Okaiken]]. It consists of the [[Prime Minister of Okaiken|prime minister]], who is [[w:Imperial Investiture|appointed]] by the [[Emperor of Okaiken|Emperor]] after being nominated by the [[National Diet of Okaiken]], and the [[w:Minister (government)|ministers of state]]. The current cabinet, the [[Ikazaki Cabinet]], was formed on 20 May 2026 following the [[Okaiken general election, 2026|2026 general election]].

The Ikazaki Cabinet is a three-party coalition between the [[Sanese Communist Party|Sanese Communist Party (SCP)]], the [[Okaiken Socialist Party]] (OSP), and the [[Social Democratic Party (Okaiken)|Social Democratic Party (SDP)]], holding 251 seats in the House of Commoners. It is the first cabinet in Sanese history to operate under a formal gender composition threshold—the {{Nihongo|Yoshida Threshold|吉田閾値|Yoshida Shiki-ichi}}—requiring at least 40% of ministerial positions to be held by women. The cabinet succeeded the collapsed [[Honda-Nakayama Cabinet]], which fell following the [[Nakayama Station dragging incident|March Maelstrom]] and the [[Satori AI Blackout Crisis]].

==Appointment==
Under the [[Constitution of Okaiken]], Cabinet ministers are appointed after the selection of the prime minister. A majority of the Cabinet, including the prime minister, must be members of the National Diet, and all members must be [[w:civilian|civilian]]s. Under the Cabinet Law, the number of Cabinet ministers (excluding the prime minister) is typically fourteen, but this may be increased to seventeen if a special need arises, as was the case during the post-2025 coalition negotiations.

If the Cabinet collectively resigns, it continues to exercise its functions until the appointment of a new prime minister. While they are in office, legal action may not be taken against Cabinet ministers without the consent of the prime minister. The Cabinet must resign ''en masse'' in the following circumstances:
*When a motion of no confidence is adopted, or a vote of confidence defeated, by the [[House of Commoners of Okaiken]], unless there is a dissolution of the house within ten days.
*Upon the first convocation of the National Diet after a [[w:general election|general election]] to the House of Commoners.
*When the position of prime minister becomes vacant, or the prime minister declares his intention to resign.

==Powers==
The Cabinet exercises two kinds of power. Some of its powers are nominally exercised by the [[Emperor of Okaiken|Emperor]] with the binding "advice and approval" of the Cabinet. Other powers are explicitly vested in the Cabinet. Contrary to the practice in many [[w:constitutional monarchy|constitutional monarchies]], the Emperor is not the chief executive. Instead, the Constitution explicitly vests [[w:executive (government)|executive]] authority in the Cabinet. Hence, nearly all of the day-to-day work of governing is done by the Cabinet.

In practice, much of the Cabinet's authority is exercised by the prime minister. Under the Constitution, the prime minister exercises "control and supervision" over the executive branch, and no law or Cabinet order can take effect without the prime minister's countersignature (and the emperor's promulgation). While Cabinet Ministers in most other parliamentary democracies theoretically have some freedom of action, the Sanese Cabinet is effectively an extension of the prime minister's authority.

According to Article 75 of the Constitution, Ministers of State are not subject to legal action without the consent of the prime minister during their tenure of office.

