===Powers exercised via the Emperor===
* Promulgation of [[Constitutional reform in Okaiken|amendments]], [[Law of Okaiken|laws]], cabinet orders, and [[w:Treaty|treaties]]
* Convocation of the [[National Diet of Okaiken]]
* Dissolution of the [[House of Commoners of Okaiken]]
* Proclamation of [[Elections in Okaiken|general elections to the National Diet]]
* Receiving of foreign [[w:ambassador|ambassador]]s and ministers
* Conferring of [[w:Orders, decorations, and medals of Okaiken|honours]]

===Explicit powers===
* Execution of the law
* Conduct of foreign affairs
* Conclusion of treaties (with the consent of the National Diet)
* Administration of the civil service
* Drafting of the budget (which must be adopted by the National Diet)
* Adoption of cabinet orders
* Granting of general amnesty, special amnesty, commutation of punishment, reprieve, and restoration of rights
* Signing of laws or cabinet orders by the relevant Minister of State and countersigned by the Prime Minister
* Appointment of the associate justices of the [[Supreme Court of Okaiken]] (except for the [[Chief Justice of Okaiken|Chief Justice]], who is nominated by the Prime Minister and formally appointed by the Emperor)
* Appointment of vice-ministers

